@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:      <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix hbco:     <http://ontosage.org/hbco#> .
@prefix ontosage: <http://ontosage.org/capabilities#> .
@prefix bldg:     <http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#> .

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Design occupancy — ONE ROOM, ONE RECORD (BUG-896, 2026-09-30)
#
# Every figure is on `hbco:roomCapacity`, the property the SHARED schema declares
# (ontology/ontosage_schema.ttl). The building used to also declare its own
# `<building>:maxOccupancy`, which meant the next building would need a different
# predicate and the system would have to guess which — design contract #3. That
# property and its triples are removed; `rec:maxOccupancy` in the Brick SHACL
# shapes is untouched.
#
# Every figure also carries `ontosage:capacityBasis`, which had ZERO triples in
# the live graph before today. The schema says why it matters: "A capacity with
# no basis cannot be told apart from a certified fire capacity, and an estimate
# quoted as a limit is a safety claim nobody made."
#
# NONE of these is certified. The enrichment file this was built from states
# "Values are approximate; authoritative data should be obtained from Estates".
# Where the two old declarations disagreed, the LOWER is recorded — exceeding a
# recorded limit is the dangerous direction — and the superseded figure is kept
# in the basis so nothing is lost and the reconciliation stays auditable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

bldg:Room1.25
    hbco:roomCapacity     20 ;
    ontosage:capacityBasis "estimated; carried forward unchanged from the building's own maxOccupancy on 2026-09-30. Not certified — Estates holds the authoritative figure." .

